# keep-pin
# E §3.1 step 1, L §6.1: "A file that doesn't match its hash is refused (LOAD-PIN)". The hash written is that of the
# member's text with rate = 0.12 (test E3_1_pin_canonical); this member states 0.13, so its canonical text differs.
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "da53b6ff6a096d47b9af5e16e8276735e72b3c343160d17d841c6ba432df1720"

ask r: a.rate
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

input rate: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.13 "umowa"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PIN ana.tally doesn't match its sha256 in use a
